# Decision tree

Agent routes from user intent **without requiring** a slash command unless the user wants the full skill ritual.

**Core routing:** [`change-control-manifest.mdc`](../change-control-manifest.mdc) § Skill routing.

**Additional intents:**

| Intent | Action |
|--------|--------|
| API / backend | `/builder-api` |
| CI/CD · IaC | `/builder-infrastructure` |
| Mobile client bug | Debug in **client repo** |
| Vault memory | `/vault-capture` · `/vault-recall` (grep-vault / Read — not directory Grep on gitignored `vault/`) |
| End-of-day | `/vault-daily` — bullets via [`vault-autolog`](./vault-autolog.mdc) |
| Multi-fix commit | One `/fix-record` per root cause |
| Unsure bug vs copy | Clarify → manifest row |

**Active mode:** patch → verify → autolog ([manifest](../change-control-manifest.mdc) step 9) · plan-only → handoff · scrutinize → no patch until approved · meta → `/upgrade-ai`.

Skill **iron law** overrides conflicting steps.
